# Both merge outputs are gitignored, not just the master. The "master"
# (messages-merged.mp4, 172MB) fails GitHub's 100MB hard per-file limit
# outright; the "-web" compressed pass (~94MB) is technically under it but
# still an oversized, unreviewed binary nobody has asked to have in git
# history. Regenerate either with build_merge.sh — see README.
public/messages-merged.mp4
public/messages-merged-web.mp4

# The labelled index cut IS committed (~25MB) — it is a useful navigable
# indexed reference copy, small enough to keep in git.
!public/messages-index.mp4
